   00001| //! Issue #918 (E71, R914-6), second migration file: the `diagnostic` prelude
   00002| //! row and the `coreference` row read only seed data in both runtimes.
   00003| //!
   00004| //! `diagnostic` recognized its per-message marker as a literal of
   00005| //! `rust/src/meta_method_dispatch.rs`. The marker is now the
   00006| //! `diagnostic_marker` table of `data/seed/handler-rules.lino`, matched in the
   00007| //! prompt itself and stripped from it, so recognition and stripping agree: an
   00008| //! upper-case marker used to be recognized in the lower-cased text but not
   00009| //! stripped from the prompt, so the inner solve met the same marker again.
   00010| //! A lower-case marker answers exactly as before.
   00011| //!
   00012| //! `coreference` already read its pronouns, antecedents and bodies from
   00013| //! `data/seed/coreference.lino`; its browser twin read only the last user turn
   00014| //! and answered only through a seeded fact. Both now resolve the nearest
   00015| //! earlier user turn naming an antecedent and answer the seeded body. The
   00016| //! browser pins are `rust/tests/web/issue-0918-handler-rules-batch-2.test.mjs`.
   00017| //!
   00018| //! `nl_tool` recognized its tool calls through seeded roles already; its seven
   00019| //! report and refusal templates are now seeded `nl_tool_*` responses. The
   00020| //! English answers below are byte-identical to the deleted format strings. The
   00021| //! refusals now speak the prompt's language (a deliberate change: a Russian
   00022| //! tool call used to be refused in English); the tool reports stay English.
   00023| //!
   00024| //! `installation_conversion` read its request cues, source and target
   00025| //! markers, prose function words and verb-to-step map from inline arrays and
   00026| //! wrote every sentence as a format string. They are now the
   00027| //! `installation_*` tables and policy of `data/seed/handler-rules.lino` and
   00028| //! seeded `installation_*` responses in both runtimes; every answer is
   00029| //! byte-identical, as the documented answers of
   00030| //! `rust/tests/unit/installation_conversion.rs` pin.
   00031| //!
   00032| //! `translation` recognized its requests through seeded roles already; its two
   00033| //! gap answers, the program-translation heading, the program gap comment and
   00034| //! the two clarifying questions of `rust/src/translation/selection.rs` are now
   00035| //! seeded English `translation_*` responses, byte-identical to the deleted
   00036| //! format strings (the gap answers stay pinned by
   00037| //! `rust/tests/unit/specification/translation_via_links.rs`).
   00038| 
